.TH EUCLID-CLI-ENS 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-ens \- manage Euclid SNS-compatible notification topics and messages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli
[\fB\-\-endpoint\fR \fIURL\fR]
[\fB\-\-loglevel\fR \fILEVEL\fR]
.B ens
.I action
[\fIaction-options\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B ens
module talks to the Euclid gateway's ens service to create and manage
SNS-compatible notification topics, publish messages to them, subscribe
EQS queues to receive fan-out deliveries, and tag topics. Every
.B ens
command sends a single JSON request to the gateway
(\fB\-\-endpoint\fR, default \fIhttps://localhost:5566\fR) and prints the
JSON response on success.
.PP
All
.B ens
commands require the caller to be authenticated; see
.B AUTHENTICATION
below for how the session used to sign these requests is obtained. There
is no administrator requirement - any authenticated user may create,
list, resolve, publish to, tag, purge and delete topics.
.PP
Some actions are still client-side only in this release - see the
.B STATUS
column below and each action's own man page for details.
.SH ACTIONS
.TP
.B create-topic
Creates a new topic with a given name and maximum message length. See
.BR euclid-cli-ens-create-topic (1).
.TP
.B list-topics
Lists topics, optionally filtered by name prefix, paged and sorted. See
.BR euclid-cli-ens-list-topics (1).
.TP
.B get-topic-ern
Resolves a topic's Euclid resource name (ERN) by its name. See
.BR euclid-cli-ens-get-topic-ern (1).
.TP
.B get-topic-metadata
Shows a topic's metadata (region, account, owner, namespace, size,
message counts). See
.BR euclid-cli-ens-get-topic-metadata (1).
.TP
.B publish-message
Publishes a message, with optional attributes, to a topic. See
.BR euclid-cli-ens-publish-message (1).
.TP
.B list-messages
Lists a topic's messages without changing their status. See
.BR euclid-cli-ens-list-messages (1).
.TP
.B get-message-count
Returns a topic's message counters (available, send, resend). See
.BR euclid-cli-ens-get-message-count (1).
.TP
.B get-message-attribute
Returns a single message attribute by key. See
.BR euclid-cli-ens-get-message-attribute (1).
.TP
.B set-message-attribute
Sets the value of a single message attribute, creating it if it doesn't
exist yet. See
.BR euclid-cli-ens-set-message-attribute (1).
.TP
.B subscribe
Subscribes a target resource (an EQS queue) to a topic, so published
messages are also delivered to it. See
.BR euclid-cli-ens-subscribe (1).
.TP
.B unsubscribe
Deletes a subscription. See
.BR euclid-cli-ens-unsubscribe (1).
.TP
.B list-subscriptions
Lists the subscriptions of a topic. See
.BR euclid-cli-ens-list-subscriptions (1).
.TP
.B add-topic-tag
Adds a tag to a topic.
.B Not yet wired to a server handler in this release.
See
.BR euclid-cli-ens-add-topic-tag (1).
.TP
.B set-topic-tag
Sets the value of an existing topic tag.
.B Not yet wired to a server handler in this release.
See
.BR euclid-cli-ens-set-topic-tag (1).
.TP
.B delete-topic-tag
Deletes a tag from a topic.
.B Not yet wired to a server handler in this release.
See
.BR euclid-cli-ens-delete-topic-tag (1).
.TP
.B purge-topic
Deletes all messages from a single topic. See
.BR euclid-cli-ens-purge-topic (1).
.TP
.B purge-all-topic
Deletes all messages from every topic in a region/account (optionally
one namespace). See
.BR euclid-cli-ens-purge-all-topic (1).
.TP
.B delete-topic
Deletes a topic by its ERN. See
.BR euclid-cli-ens-delete-topic (1).
.SH NAMES AND ERNS
Anywhere a topic is named, you may give either its plain
.B name
or its full Euclid resource name
.RB ( ERN ).
.PP
A name is resolved by the server, in the account and namespace your
session is using \- the ones recorded in
.I $HOME/.euclid/credentials
and sent with every request. So
.B datenlieferant-topic
means the topic of that name in your current namespace, and switching
namespace with
.BR euclid-cli-eam-change-namespace (1)
makes the same name refer to a different topic. That is the point of a
name: it is relative to where you are.
.PP
A full ERN is absolute, and is what you need to reach a topic in
another namespace or account \- and what every script written before
names were accepted already passes. Both forms are accepted everywhere
below; a value beginning with
.I ern:
is used as given, anything else is treated as a name.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
These options are given to
.B euclid-cli
itself, before the
.I ens
module name.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-endpoint " " \fIURL\fR
Euclid gateway endpoint to talk to, e.g. \fIhttps://localhost:5566\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-ca\-cert " " \fIPATH\fR
Path to a PEM CA certificate to trust in addition to the system trust
store, e.g. for self-signed development certificates.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
Path to a JSON configuration file providing defaults for action
options (currently used by
.BR euclid-cli-esm (1)
only). Defaults to
.IR /usr/local/euclid/etc/euclid.json ;
silently ignored if the file doesn't exist.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-signature " " \fISCHEME\fR
Signature scheme used for signed service calls: \fIsigv4\fR (the
default) or \fIrfc9421\fR for RFC 9421 HTTP Message Signatures. Both
prove the request with the same access key; RFC 9421 puts the
signature in \fISignature\fR/\fISignature\-Input\fR headers and binds
the body through \fIContent\-Digest\fR (RFC 9530) instead of using
AWS's Authorization header. Overrides
.I euclid.cli.signature
from the configuration file. Ignored for
.BR euclid-cli-eam (1)
commands, which authenticate with the session's bearer token.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-loglevel " " \fILEVEL\fR
Log level: one of \fItrace\fR, \fIdebug\fR, \fIinfo\fR, \fIwarning\fR,
\fIerror\fR, \fIfatal\fR. Defaults to \fIinfo\fR.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print top-level usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the euclid-cli version and exit.
.SH AUTHENTICATION
.B ens
commands are authenticated using the session created by
.BR euclid-cli-eam-login (1),
loaded from
.IR $HOME/.euclid/credentials .
Unlike
.B eam
commands, which always send the bearer token,
.B ens
requests are signed with SigV4 (the same scheme Euclid SDKs use for SNS)
using the access key ID and secret stored in that file, if present;
.BR euclid-cli-eam-login (1)
provisions this access key automatically on first login, so a separate
.B eam create-access-key
call is not normally needed. If no access key is stored, the bearer
token is sent instead as an
.I "Authorization: Bearer"
header.
.PP
If the server rejects a request with
.IR "HTTP 401" ,
the stored credentials are left untouched (unlike
.BR eam ,
which clears them on 401); run
.B euclid-cli eam login
again if requests start failing with 401.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The action completed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
Argument parsing failed, the request could not be sent, or the server
rejected it (missing/expired session, invalid input, topic not found,
action not implemented, etc.). Details are printed to standard error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $HOME/.euclid/credentials
JSON file holding the current session's bearer token and/or SigV4
access key, created by
.B euclid-cli eam login
and read by every
.B ens
action.
.SH EXAMPLES
Create a topic, resolve its ERN, and publish a message to it:
.PP
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 ens create-topic \e
    --name order-events --max-length 65536

euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 ens get-topic-ern \e
    --name order-events

euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 ens publish-message \e
    --topic ern:ens:eu-central-1:000000000000:topic:order-events \e
    --body '{"orderId": "42", "status": "shipped"}'
.fi
.RE
.PP
Subscribe a queue to a topic, then remove the subscription:
.PP
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 ens subscribe \e
    --source-ern ern:ens:eu-central-1:000000000000:topic:order-events \e
    --target-ern ern:eqs:eu-central-1:000000000000:queue:orders

euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 ens unsubscribe \e
    --subscription ern:ens:eu-central-1:000000000000:subscription:6f1b1e2e...
.fi
.RE
.PP
List every topic, inspect one topic's messages, then delete the topic:
.PP
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 ens list-topics

euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 ens list-messages \e
    --topic ern:ens:eu-central-1:000000000000:topic:order-events

euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 ens delete-topic \e
    --topic ern:ens:eu-central-1:000000000000:topic:order-events
.fi
.RE
